course: dictionary
lesson: 9682
title: Sue: a verb and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sue has two jobs in English. As a verb, to sue someone means to go to a court of law and ask for money or justice, because they harmed you or broke an agreement. «The family sued the company» tells you the family took the company to court.
explain: Context clues show you which meaning you need. A capital S in the middle of a sentence, and words like Aunt or Auntie before it, tell you Sue is a person's name. «Aunt Sue hands over a goldfish» is about a person, not a court case.
explain: A quick check helps. Swap in "took to court" for the verb. If the sentence still makes sense, sue is the verb. If it only makes sense as a person, Sue is the name.
explain: The verb changes with time: sue, sues, sued, suing. Use sued for the past, as in «some AI music companies were sued». Use sues with he, she or it, as in «she sues the shop».
fact: To sue means to go to a court of law to ask for money or justice.
fact: People sue when someone has harmed them or broken an agreement.
fact: Judges in a court settle disagreements fairly, and suing is one way to use them.
fact: Sue, with a capital S, is a girl's name, short for Susan.
fact: «Sue» is a famous T. rex skeleton in the Field Museum in Chicago, named after Sue Hendrickson, who found it in South Dakota in 1990.
exercise: «The family sued the company.» What does sued mean here? | Bought a new car for the company | Waved goodbye at the door | *Went to a court of law to ask for money or justice
exercise: «Aunt Sue hands over a goldfish at the fair.» What kind of word is Sue here? | *A name, short for Susan | A type of bag | A verb, meaning to go to court
exercise: In «Auntie Sue», what clue tells you Sue is a name? | The word goldfish after it | *The capital S, and Auntie in front of it | The word fair at the end of the sentence | The word hands before it
test: In «Sue, one of the largest T. rex skeletons, was found in South Dakota in 1990», what is Sue? | A verb meaning to go to court | A town in South Dakota | *The name of a skeleton
test: Which word fits? «Yesterday, the families ___ the company.» | *sued | sues | suing
exam: What does sued mean in «major record labels reportedly sued some AI music companies»? | *Went to a court of law to ask for money or justice | Sang a song about music | Gave the companies a prize
